UPDATE companies SET description='PwrQ operates from Hanover, Maryland, tracing its roots to 1926. The company is now a subsidiary of Forgent, which brought together over a century of power‑systems experience to address modern infrastructure challenges. No individual founders are named in the available sources.

The firm designs and manufactures low‑voltage power distribution equipment — including S1 switchboards, remote power panels (RPP), panelboards, power distribution units (PDU), and automatic transfer switches — through vertically integrated facilities that handle copper busbar fabrication, CNC turret punching, laser cutting, robotic welding, and final assembly and test. Dedicated production lanes for each product family enable high‑volume, high‑precision output. In‑house electrical and application engineering teams perform power‑systems engineering, reliability studies, short‑circuit coordination, arc‑flash analysis, and SCADA/BMS integration. Field services cover preventive maintenance, inspection and testing of medium‑ and low‑voltage switchgear, breakers, relays, and transformers, as well as generator solutions ranging from 3 kW to 10 MW with paralleling and microgrid controls.

PwrQ serves hyperscale data centers, manufacturing plants, utility grids, hospital campuses, and other mission‑critical industrial facilities where uptime and scalability are essential. Its engineering approach spans the full single‑line diagram from utility entrance to rack‑level load, and its service teams are strategically positioned for national and global response.', certifications=ARRAY['UL LISTED']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Power systems engineering", "Reliability studies", "Short circuit coordination", "Arc flash studies", "Switchgear controls and automation", "SCADA/BMS implementation and integration", "Generator paralleling", "Hybrid microgrid controls", "Preventive maintenance agreements", "Inspection and testing of MV/LV switchgear, breakers, relays, transformers", "Startup and commissioning", "Retrofits and upgrades", "Controls integration", "CNC turret punching", "Laser cutting", "Robotic welding", "Automated copper busbar processing", "Final assembly and test", "Raw material processing", "Dedicated production lane manufacturing", "Field services (emergency response, system upgrades)", "Generator maintenance", "Training programs"], "industries": ["Hyperscale data centers", "Manufacturing facilities", "Power grid / utilities", "Hospital campuses", "High-demand industrial facilities", "Mission-critical environments"], "materials": ["Copper busbar"], "equipment": ["CNC turret punches", "Laser cutters", "Robotic welders", "Automated copper processing systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated manufacturing from raw material to final test", "Dedicated production lanes per product family for speed and consistency", "Advanced automation including CNC turret punches, laser cutters, robotic welders, and AI\u2011driven copper processing", "In\u2011house engineering covering the complete single\u2011line diagram", "Full lifecycle field services including preventive maintenance, retrofits, and generat