UPDATE companies SET description='Randy''s Booth Co. Inc. operates from a renovated facility in Crystal, Minnesota, a northwest suburb of Minneapolis. The business traces its roots to the 1970s when Randy Kissoondath, an immigrant from Trinidad and Tobago, began building restaurant booths and earned a national reputation for custom seating. After a health-related sale and a later restart, Randy''s son Bert Kissoondath joined the company in his mid-20s, learning every aspect of production before assuming leadership following his father''s sudden death in 2009. The firm relocated to its current 2-acre site in September 2017, gaining 20-foot ceiling clearance, a loading dock, and a showroom.

The company manufactures custom hospitality furnishings—booths, banquettes, chairs, stools, tables, and headboards—using Northern Hardwoods such as cherry, ash, oak, and maple. A 20-person team handles design, fabrication, finishing, and installation in-house, allowing the shop to control quality from raw lumber to final placement. While the earlier iteration employed 40 people serving chains like Hyatt and Perkins, the current operation focuses on a close-knit crew that manages projects from concept through installation.

Customers include restaurant groups, designers, architects, and healthcare and corporate clients across the United States. Recent projects range from multi-unit restaurant build-outs for operators such as Nova Restaurant Group (Hazelwood Food & Drink) and independent owners (Stanley''s NE, Pub 819, The Howe Daily Kitchen and Bar) to the Super Bowl celebration at the Minneapolis Armory, where the shop delivered custom walls, poster panels, tables, and seating on a tight timeline.

The company emphasizes generational craftsmanship and a "customized craft in a cut-and-paste world" philosophy. Bert Kissoondath cites his father''s lesson that pride in work shows in the finished product, a principle that earned the firm the 2024 Minnesota Manufacturer of the Year award and the SBA''s Minnesota Family Owned Business of the Year honor. The leadership team highlights on-time delivery, value engineering, and direct oversight of every installation as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom booth manufacturing", "Banquette manufacturing", "Chair manufacturing", "Stool manufacturing", "Table and base manufacturing", "Headboard manufacturing", "Custom furniture design", "Woodworking (Northern Hardwoods)", "Finishing and staining", "Installation services", "Project management", "Value engineering"], "industries": ["Hospitality (restaurants, lounges)", "Healthcare", "Corporate offices", "Residential", "Commercial seating"], "materials": ["Cherry", "Ash", "Oak", "Maple", "Northern Hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house design, fabrication, and installation", "Nationwide delivery with on-site installation oversight", "Value engineering for cost optimization", "Second-generation family ownership", "2024 Minnesota Manufacturer of the Year"], "facts_used": ["Randy Kissoondath founded the business in the 1970s after immigrating from Trinidad and Tobago -> /about-us", "Bert Kissoondath became CEO after his father''s death in 2009 -> /about-us", "Company moved to Crystal, MN in September 2017 -> /about-us", "Current headcount is 20 employees -> /about-us", "Manufactures custom booths, chairs, tables from Northern Hardwoods (Cherry, Ash, Oak, Maple) -> /", "Serves hospitality, healthcare, corporate, and residential markets -> /", "Awarded 2024 Minnesota Manufacturer of the Year -> /", "Named 2024 Minnesota Family Owned Business of the Year by SBA -> /about-us", "Provides design, build, and installation services -> /about-us", "Historical clients include Hyatt and Perkins -> /about-us", "Projects include Hazelwood Food & Drink and Super Bowl Armory celebration -> /, /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our work includes high quality, expertly designed commercial booths, chairs, and tables made from Northern Hardwoods such as Cherry, Ash, Oak and Maple.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "20", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='randy-s-booth-co-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ray Brothers Inc., operating as Ray Bros., Inc., is an architectural sheet metal fabricator based in New Orleans, Louisiana. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed, nor are its founders named in available sources.

The firm produces structural and architectural metal panels—including its MT240, M100, and 200 series—along with framing products and custom fabrications. Its shop offers waterjet cutting, press forming, and custom fabrication services, and it also provides commercial general contracting, material sales, and project planning, estimating, and design. Facility size, headcount, and production volumes are not published.

Ray Bros. serves commercial, institutional, and government construction markets. Completed projects include re-roofing the Nashville Avenue Terminal at the Port of New Orleans, retro-framing the Plaquemines Parish Council Building, copper roofing for the Old Algiers Courthouse and Holy Name of Mary Catholic Church, and work on Fifth Ward Elementary, Slidell Government Tower, and the Louisiana Avenue Wharf.

