UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Pine Ridge, South Dakota, Red Cloud Renewable Energy Center operates as a 501(c)(3) nonprofit dedicated to advancing energy sovereignty in Native American communities. The organization’s founding date and original founders are not publicly disclosed, but its mission centers on providing free, hands-on training in solar installation, weatherization, and sustainable building practices.

The center’s core activity is a workforce development program that combines classroom instruction with field work: each training cohort installs photovoltaic systems on homes of families identified as needing assistance most. This dual approach builds technical skills while delivering immediate energy cost reductions. The curriculum covers photovoltaic system design, safety protocols, and weatherization techniques aimed at improving home resilience in harsh climates. No facility size, headcount, or annual installation volume is published.

Red Cloud Renewable serves Native American students seeking careers in the green energy sector, as well as low-income households on reservations who receive the installed systems. Its work aligns with the broader renewable energy and weatherization industries, and the organization explicitly frames its impact under the banner of ''Support Energy Sovereignty.'' Testimonials from program graduates highlight career placement and personal empowerment.

The organization states that its model is a ''new way to honor the old ways,'' linking cultural values with modern sustainability. By offering training at no cost and coupling it with direct community installations, it aims to foster self-sufficiency, lower energy bills, and reduce carbon emissions—each kilowatt installed is said to prevent roughly 1.5 tons of CO2 annually.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar photovoltaic installation training", "Weatherization training", "Sustainable building practices education", "Residential solar panel installation (as part of training)", "Workforce development for renewable energy careers"], "industries": ["Support Energy Sovereignty", "Renewable energy", "Weatherization", "Solar energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One donation funds three outcomes: free solar training for Native students, a residential installation for a family in need, and measurable carbon reduction.", "Training cohorts perform real-world installations as part of their curriculum.", "Program focuses on energy sovereignty for Native American communities.", "501(c)(3) nonprofit status ensures mission-driven operation."], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Pine Ridge, South Dakota -> db", "Organization type: 501(c)(3) nonprofit -> /", "Mission: empowers Native American communities through education in solar installation, weatherization, sustainable building -> /, /about", "Free training for Native students in solar installation -> /", "Each class installs panels for families in need -> /", "Environmental impact: each kW solar prevents ~1.5 tons CO2 per year -> /", "Testimonials from program graduates (Rachael La Friniere, Gail Hubbeling, Keva New Holy) -> /", "BRIDGE program mentioned -> /", "Industries served: Support Energy Sovereignty -> db", "Website: https://www.redcloudrenewable.org/ -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Red Cloud Renewable is a 501(c)(3) organization that empowers Native American communities by offering vital education in solar installation and weatherization techniques.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='red-cloud-renewable-energy-center' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Redstone Solar is a solar energy installation company based in Provo, Utah. The firm provides residential and commercial solar panel and battery storage systems across Utah County, including projects in Provo and Orem.

