ices", "Proprietary inventory management system for 50+ years -> /services", "Over 130 active retrofit codes -> /services", "Custom garments with extremely low minimums -> /services", "Materials: poly\u2011cotton, 100% cotton, GlenGuard FR, 7.2 oz spun poly -> /", "ANSI certification -> db", "Industries: food service, industrial safety, FR workwear, enhanced visibility -> /, /about", "Wholesale distributor network -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "REED has designed and manufactured high quality, comfortable, protective workwear since 1919.", "founded_year": "1919", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "Extremely low minimums for custom garments", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned", "Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='reed-manufacturing-co-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Reeves Custom Metals operates from Wichita, Kansas, where the Reeves family has provided metal services in the Delano district for five generations. The business traces its roots to 1897, when Reeves Brothers Blacksmith Shop opened (now West Douglas). The current facility sits one block north of that original site

The shop delivers full-service custom metal fabrication, including welding (MIG, TIG, arc, and gas), cutting (high-definition plasma, laser, waterjet, tube laser, flame, and shearing), and forming (press brake, sheet rolling, hand brake, English wheel, power hammer, and CNC tube bending). It also offers CNC plasma shape cutting, sawing to length, AutoCAD design, general machine repair, and finishing. The company stocks a broad inventory of carbon steel, stainless steel, aluminum, copper, brass, and specialty alloys, plus remnants, with no minimum order requirement.

Reeves serves a range of industries that require custom metalwork, from structural fabrication to precision components.

