UPDATE companies SET description='Renaissance Design Group operates from St. Cloud, Minnesota, where craftsman Mike Fanslau launched the operation in 2018 with the purchase of a Timberking portable sawmill.

The company transforms salvaged logs into custom furniture, small structures, and architectural lumber. Fanslau builds he-sheds, she-sheds, outhouses, pet shelters, benches, and a range of epoxy-finished pieces such as coffee tables, mantels, bar tops, and memory tables. The shop also offers epoxy mentorship and a la carte milling services for DIY customers.

Customers include homeowners preserving sentimental trees, residential builders sourcing lumber from lot clearing, and commercial projects seeking Carbon Smart Wood—architectural-grade material from urban salvage. The company picks up downed logs with a hoisted trailer and maintains a rotating inventory of Minnesota hardwoods (oak, ash, maple, walnut, cherry) and softwoods (pine, spruce, fir, tamarack).

