UPDATE companies SET description='Revelation Medical Devices was founded in 1976 in Auburn, Indiana, and has operated continuously from that location for nearly five decades. The company began as a supplier of medical instrumentation to the orthopaedic industry and has expanded its capabilities over time.

Today the firm provides end-to-end medical device contract manufacturing, covering design, development, prototyping, and production. Its shop runs 3-, 4-, and 5-axis milling, live-tool turning, orthopaedic-quality finishing, a dedicated plastics manufacturing cell, laser and TIG welding, laser etching, passivation, polishing, and non-sterile packaging and labeling. The facility serves projects from prototype through full-scale production, though specific headcount and floor space are not disclosed.

Customers include large and small orthopaedic OEMs as well as medical-device startups. The company emphasizes its proximity to Warsaw, Indiana — known as the orthopaedic capital — which allows close collaboration with clients in that cluster.

Revelation Medical Devices states that its mission is to empower medical device innovators through ISO-certified, high-precision manufacturing delivered with reliability, flexibility, and excellence. Core values cited are excellence, integrity, teamwork, and compassion, and the company highlights its FDA registration and ISO 13485:2016 certification as foundations of its quality system.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Multi-axis milling (3, 4, 5-axis)", "Live tool turning", "Orthopaedic quality finishing", "Dedicated poly/plastic manufacturing cell", "Laser welding", "TIG welding", "Laser etching", "Passivation", "Polishing", "Non-sterile packaging and labeling", "Medical device design", "Medical device development", "Prototyping", "Production manufacturing"], "industries": ["Orthopaedic", "Medical Device OEMs", "Medical Device Startups"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 13485:2016 certified and FDA registered (Registration Number 1836116)", "Prototype-to-production capabilities including 3/4/5-axis milling, live-tool turning, and orthopaedic finishing", "Dedicated plastics/polymer manufacturing cell", "Laser and TIG welding, laser etching, passivation, and polishing in-house", "Located within 45 minutes of Warsaw, IN, the orthopaedic industry hub"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1976 in Auburn, Indiana -> db, /about", "ISO 13485:2016 certified -> /", "FDA Registration Number 1836116 -> /", "Capabilities: 3/4/5-axis milling, live tool turning, orthopaedic finishing, plastics cell, laser/TIG welding, laser etching, passivation, polishing, non-sterile packaging -> /", "Serves orthopaedic industry, medical device OEMs and startups -> /, /about", "Mission: empower medical device innovators with ISO-certified high precision manufacturing -> /about", "Located within 45 minutes of Warsaw, IN -> /", "Company type: contract manufacturer -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Why Choose RMD for Medical Device Contract Manufacturing?", "founded_year": "1976", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/revelation-medical-devices/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='revelation-medical-devices' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company began by supplying efficient irrigation solutions to farmers in the Mid-South region and quickly added recycling operations to address plastic waste. In 2008 the business expanded to Little Rock, where it established its first sustainable-loop recycling facility and launched the Revolution Bag line of trash can liners made with up to 97% certified post-consumer resin. The headquarters remain in Little Rock, Arkansas.

Today Revolution manufactures a range of plastic products including trash can liners, carryout bags for foodservice and retail, agricultural films, commercial sheeting, and stretch films. The company runs an integrated circular model: a specialized fleet collects used film, which is cleaned and mechanically recycled at its facilities to produce certified post-consumer and post-industrial resins. Those resins feed both Revolution’s own product lines and the supply chains of global brands and OEMs. The company reports processing more than 300 million pounds of material annually and has diverted over 3 billion pounds from landfills since inception. Growth has come through acquisitions such as Rodeo Plastic Bag & Film, Command Packaging, Encore Recycling, Pak-Sher, Polar Plastics, Jadcore, and Five Point Films, adding capacity in commercial films, consumer bags, post-industrial recycling, and stretch films.

Revolution serves agriculture, food service, construction and commercial supply, consumer goods, restaurants, delis, and grocery chains. Its recycled resins are sold to brands and original equipment manufacturers seeking circular content. A noted reference comes from Hartsfield-Jackson Atlanta International Airport, where a sustainability manager reported reducing virgin resin use from hundreds of thousands of pounds to 17,000 pounds annually through Revolution’s programs.

The company was started to demonstrate that plastic can be a valuable resource with infinite usefulness if reclaimed responsibly. Its stated differentiator is a closed-loop business model that controls the entire lifecycle — from collection and recycling to resin production and finished goods — enabling customers to meet ESG goals while maintaining product performance.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Film collection and logistics", "Mechanical recycling of flexible films", "Recycled resin production (post-consumer and post-industrial)", "Sustainable product manufacturing (trash can liners, carryout bags, agricultural films, commercial sheeting, stretch films)", "Custom sustainable loop program development", "Irrigation planning software (Pipe Planner)"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Food service", "Construction", "Commercial supply", "Consumer goods", "Restaurant", "Deli", "Grocery", "Scrap recycling", "OEMs", "Brands"], "materials": ["Post-consumer resin (PCR)", "Post-industrial resin", "Polyethylene film", "Agricultural film", "Plastic scrap"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Integrated circular business model controlling the full plastic lifecycle", "In-house collection and mechanical recycling of over 300 million pounds of film per year", "Products manufactured with up to 100% certified post-consumer resin", "Proprietary recycling process for heavily soiled agricultural films", "Custom sustainable loop programs for brands and OEMs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 in Stuttgart, Arkansas -> /about", "Headquarters in Little Rock, Arkansas -> db", "Processes over 300 million pounds of material annually -> /", "Diverted 3 billion pounds from landfills -> /", "Manufactures products with up to 100% post-consumer resin -> /", "Offers film collection and mechanical recycling -> /services", "Serves agriculture, food service, construction, consumer, restaurant, deli, grocery -> /about", "Acquisitions: Rodeo Plastic Bag & Film, Command Packaging, Encore Recycling, Pak-Sher, Polar Plastics, Jadcore, Five Point Films -> /about", "Operates divisions: Sustainable Agriculture, Sustainable Commercial, Sustainable Consumer, Sustainable Materials, Sustainable Stretch Solutions -> /about", "Provides custom sustainable loop programs for brands and OEMs -> /services", "Uses proprietary mechanical recycling process for heavily soiled ag films -> /services", "Pipe Planner irrigation software saves 100 billion gallons water annually -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We manufacture products with up to 100% post-consumer resin.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='revolution-bag' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Reworx operates from Morris, Connecticut, with a shop in Watertown and a studio on Watertown Road in Morris.

The business designs and builds custom furniture and accents — such as reclaimed barn‑wood mantels — using salvaged lumber and other reclaimed stock. Services include a design studio where clients collaborate with reclamation experts, direct sales of salvaged wood for DIY projects, and a mobile on‑site design and installation consultation service for residential and commercial spaces.

The salvage and wood sales channel also caters to DIY enthusiasts looking for reclaimed material for their own projects.

